diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 3870b72..6dd4e2e 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -95,3 +95,4 @@ Entering the page reads the cache again only when it is entered (`dedupEnter` no
 - `Painter.AnimationFrame` (and `After`) only paints the window again: the view is not built, so anything computed while building (an element's size, an effect's uniforms, state moved on in `View`) stands still in those frames. Read the time as you paint (`p.Now()` in a `Draw` callback, or in an effect's `PaintEffect`, as `specksFx` does), and call `c.Invalidate()` while something built must move (`a.moving()`). Stamp an animation's start in the first frame that shows it, not from the last frame built, which may be long past.
 - Files come and go through specks (`app/arrivals.go`): a deleted file stays in its listing while it dissolves (`a.dying`, kept through reloads by `keepDying`), and an upload shows in its folder at once as a row with a negative FsID that gathers as its bytes go up (`a.gathers`, by the path of the entry it makes); rows with a negative FsID or dissolving are never chosen or opened.
 - Sidebar icons are drawn in code (`app/navicons.go`) so their parts can move; `navGlyph` takes the time into the gesture. A page's icon plays once when the page opens (`a.navRun`).
+- The browser's rubber-band selection (`marquee` in `app/browser.go`): pressing the primary button in the list or grid and dragging paints a rounded rectangle from the press point to the pointer with `page.DrawOver` — a faint `t.Accent.Alpha(0.12)` fill and a 1px `t.Accent` stroke — clipped to the list's or grid's viewport (`l.dragArea`). The press comes from the page's `ObserveInput`, so a drag begun in a row's blank space counts too and the box ends on the release; the list's rows are still chosen by MyGo's `ListState.DragSelecting` (`DragSelect`), which the rectangle only mirrors, while the grid chooses the tiles whose `gridSpot.rect` the rectangle intersects. It is hidden while the preview, a dialog, an in-place rename or the folder maker has the pointer, and while files from another app are dragged in (`l.over`).
